-- Sale of Goods Act 1979 (Singapore), 2020 RE, informal consolidation in force from 1/4/2022.
-- LAYER 1, PART 7: SUPPLEMENTARY (ss 55 to 60, 62; s 58 is omitted; s 61 is in soga-interpretation; s 63 is the short title).
-- The auction duties of s 57(4) are also written as a regulative rule in soga-duties; the decision functions here are its twins.
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE are answers the text gives in its own words; NOTHING is "the Act does not answer on
-- these facts".  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `soga-nouns`

DECLARE `Way of negativing or varying a right, duty or liability implied by law` IS ONE OF
    `express agreement`
    `the course of dealing between the parties`
    `such usage as binds both parties to the contract`
    `some other way`

DECLARE `Matter an auction sale may be notified or reserved` IS ONE OF
    `a reserve or upset price`
    `a right to bid expressly reserved by or on behalf of the seller`
    `some other matter an auction sale may be notified or reserved`

DECLARE `Matter on which section 62 speaks` IS ONE OF
    `the rules in bankruptcy relating to contracts of sale`
    `the enactments relating to bills of sale`
    `some other matter under section 62(3)`

§ `Part 7 -- Supplementary`

§§ `Exclusion of implied terms (s 55) and conflict of laws (s 56)`

-- s 55(1).
-- src:1454 | 55.—(1) Where a right, duty or liability would arise under a
-- src:1455 | contract of sale of goods by implication of law, it may (subject to the
-- src:1456 | Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977) be negatived or varied by express
-- src:1457 | agreement, or by the course of dealing between the parties, or by such
-- src:1458 | usage as binds both parties to the contract.
@ref s 55(1) (src:1454-1458)
GIVEN `a right, duty or liability would arise under a contract of sale of goods by implication of law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 prevents the negativing or variation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the way` IS A `Way of negativing or varying a right, duty or liability implied by law`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 55(1) the right, duty or liability may be negatived or varied` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a right, duty or liability would arise under a contract of sale of goods by implication of law`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection applies "Where a right, duty or liability would arise under a contract of sale of goods by implication of law". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 prevents the negativing or variation`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "(subject to the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977)"; that Act is not among the sources.
            NOTHING
        IF `the way` EQUALS `express agreement` OR `the way` EQUALS `the course of dealing between the parties` OR `the way` EQUALS `such usage as binds both parties to the contract`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection names three ways and does not say that no other way will do.
            NOTHING

-- s 55(2).
-- src:1460 | (2) An express condition or warranty does not negative a condition
-- src:1461 | or warranty implied by this Act unless inconsistent with it.
@ref s 55(2) (src:1460-1461)
GIVEN `the express condition or warranty is inconsistent with the condition or warranty implied by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 55(2) an express condition or warranty negatives a condition or warranty implied by this Act` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the express condition or warranty is inconsistent with the condition or warranty implied by this Act`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless inconsistent with it" -- the subsection says only when an express term does not negative; it does not say that an inconsistent one does.
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An express condition or warranty does not negative a condition or warranty implied by this Act unless inconsistent with it."
            -- MARGINAL (a): "unless" is read as the text's no when the express term is not inconsistent.
            JUST FALSE

-- s 55(3), paragraph 9.
-- src:1466 | (3) Paragraph 9 of the Schedule applies in relation to a contract
-- src:1467 | made on or after 18 May 1973 and before 1 February 1978, and
-- src:1468 | paragraph 10 in relation to one made before 18 May 1973.
@ref s 55(3) para 9 (src:1466-1468)
GIVEN `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 55(3) paragraph 9 of the Schedule applies in relation to the contract` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the date the contract was made` AT LEAST (Date 18 5 1973)) AND (NOT (`the date the contract was made` AT LEAST (Date 1 2 1978)))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph 9 applies "in relation to a contract made on or after 18 May 1973 and before 1 February 1978"; for another contract paragraph 9 does not apply. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE

-- s 55(3), paragraph 10.
-- src:1466 | (3) Paragraph 9 of the Schedule applies in relation to a contract
-- src:1467 | made on or after 18 May 1973 and before 1 February 1978, and
-- src:1468 | paragraph 10 in relation to one made before 18 May 1973.
@ref s 55(3) para 10 (src:1466-1468)
GIVEN `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 55(3) paragraph 10 of the Schedule applies in relation to the contract` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the date the contract was made` AT LEAST (Date 18 5 1973))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph 10 applies "in relation to one made before 18 May 1973"; for another contract paragraph 10 does not apply. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE

-- s 56.
-- src:1472 | 56. Paragraph 11 of the Schedule applies in relation to a contract
-- src:1473 | made on or after 18 May 1973 and before 1 February 1978, so as to
-- src:1474 | make provision about conflict of laws in relation to such a contract.
@ref s 56 (src:1472-1474)
GIVEN `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 56 paragraph 11 of the Schedule applies in relation to the contract` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the date the contract was made` AT LEAST (Date 18 5 1973)) AND (NOT (`the date the contract was made` AT LEAST (Date 1 2 1978)))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph 11 applies "in relation to a contract made on or after 18 May 1973 and before 1 February 1978"; paragraph 11(2) itself says to ignore section 56 for any other contract. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE

§§ `Auction sales (s 57)`

-- s 57(1).
-- src:1478 | 57.—(1) Where goods are put up for sale by auction in lots, each lot
-- src:1479 | is prima facie deemed to be the subject of a separate contract of sale.
@ref s 57(1) (src:1478-1479)
GIVEN `goods are put up for sale by auction in lots` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is shown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 57(1) each lot is deemed to be the subject of a separate contract of sale` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `goods are put up for sale by auction in lots`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where goods are put up for sale by auction in lots, each lot is prima facie deemed to be the subject of a separate contract of sale" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if".
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the contrary is shown`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "prima facie" -- the deeming yields to proof of the contrary, and the subsection does not say what follows then.
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 57(2), completion.
-- src:1481 | (2) A sale by auction is complete when the auctioneer announces its
-- src:1482 | completion by the fall of the hammer, or in other customary manner;
-- src:1483 | and until the announcement is made any bidder may retract his bid.
@ref s 57(2) complete (src:1481-1483)
GIVEN `the auctioneer announces the completion of the sale by the fall of the hammer, or in other customary manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 57(2) the sale by auction is complete` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the auctioneer announces the completion of the sale by the fall of the hammer, or in other customary manner`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A sale by auction is complete when the auctioneer announces its completion"; until the announcement is made the sale is not complete ("when" read as "where": fork F10). -- ruled 2026-11-05 (w): "when" read as "where" (ruled 2026-11-05: "when" counts as "where"; fork F10): the condition not met is the text's no
            JUST FALSE

-- s 57(2), retraction.
-- src:1481 | (2) A sale by auction is complete when the auctioneer announces its
-- src:1482 | completion by the fall of the hammer, or in other customary manner;
-- src:1483 | and until the announcement is made any bidder may retract his bid.
@ref s 57(2) retract (src:1481-1483)
GIVEN `the auctioneer has announced the completion of the sale` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 57(2) any bidder may retract his bid` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the auctioneer has announced the completion of the sale`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the announcement is made any bidder may retract his bid" is a stated period; after the announcement no bidder may retract under this subsection. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE

-- s 57(3).
-- src:1485 | (3) A sale by auction may be notified to be subject to a reserve or
-- src:1486 | upset price, and a right to bid may also be reserved expressly by or on
-- src:1487 | behalf of the seller.
@ref s 57(3) (src:1485-1487)
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `Matter an auction sale may be notified or reserved`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 57(3) the sale by auction may be notified to be subject to, or a right may be reserved in respect of, this matter` IS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `a reserve or upset price` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a right to bid expressly reserved by or on behalf of the seller` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection says a sale "may be" notified in these ways and does not say that no other is allowed.
    WHEN `some other matter an auction sale may be notified or reserved` THEN NOTHING

-- s 57(4), the seller.
-- src:1489 | (4) Where a sale by auction is not notified to be subject to a right to
-- src:1490 | bid by or on behalf of the seller, it is not lawful for the seller to bid
-- src:1491 | himself or to employ any person to bid at the sale, or for the
-- src:1492 | auctioneer knowingly to take any bid from the seller or any such
-- src:1493 | person.
@ref s 57(4) seller (src:1489-1493)
GIVEN `the sale by auction is notified to be subject to a right to bid by or on behalf of the seller` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 57(4) it is lawful for the seller to bid himself or to employ any person to bid at the sale` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the sale by auction is notified to be subject to a right to bid by or on behalf of the seller`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not lawful for the seller to bid himself or to employ any person to bid at the sale"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition applies "Where a sale by auction is not notified to be subject to a right to bid by or on behalf of the seller"; s 57(6) deals with the case where the right is reserved.
            NOTHING

-- s 57(4), the auctioneer.
-- src:1489 | (4) Where a sale by auction is not notified to be subject to a right to
-- src:1490 | bid by or on behalf of the seller, it is not lawful for the seller to bid
-- src:1491 | himself or to employ any person to bid at the sale, or for the
-- src:1492 | auctioneer knowingly to take any bid from the seller or any such
-- src:1493 | person.
@ref s 57(4) auctioneer (src:1489-1493)
GIVEN `the sale by auction is notified to be subject to a right to bid by or on behalf of the seller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auctioneer knows that the bid is from the seller or a person employed by the seller to bid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 57(4) it is lawful for the auctioneer to take the bid` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the sale by auction is notified to be subject to a right to bid by or on behalf of the seller`) AND `the auctioneer knows that the bid is from the seller or a person employed by the seller to bid`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not lawful ... for the auctioneer knowingly to take any bid from the seller or any such person"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition covers only a bid the auctioneer "knowingly" takes, in a sale not notified to be subject to a right to bid.
            NOTHING

-- s 57(5).
-- src:1495 | (5) A sale contravening subsection (4) may be treated as fraudulent
-- src:1496 | by the buyer.
@ref s 57(5) (src:1495-1496)
GIVEN `the sale contravenes subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 57(5) the sale may be treated as fraudulent by the buyer` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the sale contravenes subsection (4)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection applies to "A sale contravening subsection (4)".
            NOTHING

-- s 57(6).
-- src:1498 | (6) Where, in respect of a sale by auction, a right to bid is expressly
-- src:1499 | reserved (but not otherwise) the seller or any one person on his behalf
-- src:1500 | may bid at the auction.
@ref s 57(6) (src:1498-1500)
GIVEN `a right to bid is expressly reserved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller bids himself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of persons who bid on his behalf` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 57(6) the seller, or any one person on his behalf, may bid at the auction` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a right to bid is expressly reserved`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, in respect of a sale by auction, a right to bid is expressly reserved (but not otherwise)"
            JUST FALSE
        IF (`the seller bids himself` AND `the number of persons who bid on his behalf` EQUALS 0) OR ((NOT `the seller bids himself`) AND `the number of persons who bid on his behalf` EQUALS 1)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is to "the seller or any one person on his behalf"; it does not say what follows if the seller and an agent both bid, or if more than one agent bids.
            -- MARGINAL (b): "the seller or any one person" is read as a limited grant, not as the text's no.
            NOTHING

§§ `Reasonable time, enforcement by action, and savings (ss 59, 60 and 62)`

-- s 59.
-- src:1506 | 59. Where a reference is made in this Act to a reasonable time, the
-- src:1507 | question what is a reasonable time is a question of fact.
@ref s 59 (src:1506-1507)
GIVEN `a reference is made in this Act to a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 59 what is a reasonable time is a question of fact` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `a reference is made in this Act to a reasonable time`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the section applies "Where a reference is made in this Act to a reasonable time". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 60.
-- src:1514 | 60. Where a right, duty or liability is declared by this Act, it may,
-- src:1515 | unless otherwise provided by this Act, be enforced by action.
@ref s 60 (src:1514-1515)
GIVEN `a right, duty or liability is declared by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this Act otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 60 the right, duty or liability may be enforced by action` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a right, duty or liability is declared by this Act`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the section applies "Where a right, duty or liability is declared by this Act". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE
        IF `this Act otherwise provides`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless otherwise provided by this Act" -- the other provision decides.
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 62(1).
-- src:1625 | 62.—(1) The rules in bankruptcy relating to contracts of sale apply
-- src:1626 | to those contracts, notwithstanding anything in this Act.
@ref s 62(1) (src:1625-1626)
GIVEN `the contract is a contract of sale` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 62(1) the rules in bankruptcy relating to contracts of sale apply to the contract notwithstanding anything in this Act` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the contract is a contract of sale`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "contracts of sale".
            NOTHING

-- s 62(2).
-- src:1628 | (2) The rules of the common law, including the law merchant,
-- src:1629 | except in so far as they are inconsistent with the provisions of this
-- src:1630 | Act, and in particular the rules relating to the law of principal and
-- src:1631 | agent and the effect of fraud, misrepresentation, duress or coercion,
-- src:1632 | mistake, or other invalidating cause, apply to contracts for the sale of
-- src:1633 | goods.
@ref s 62(2) (src:1628-1633)
GIVEN `the contract is a contract for the sale of goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rule of the common law is inconsistent with the provisions of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 62(2) the rule of the common law applies to the contract` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the contract is a contract for the sale of goods`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "contracts for the sale of goods".
            NOTHING
        IF `the rule of the common law is inconsistent with the provisions of this Act`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The rules of the common law, including the law merchant, except in so far as they are inconsistent with the provisions of this Act ... apply to contracts for the sale of goods."
            -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "except in so far as" is read as the text's no; the other reading is that "except in so far as" states an exception only and the text is silent when it fails.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 62(3).
-- src:1635 | (3) Nothing in this Act affects the enactments relating to bills of
-- src:1636 | sale.
@ref s 62(3) (src:1635-1636)
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `Matter on which section 62 speaks`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 62(3) this Act affects the matter` IS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (3) says nothing about the rules in bankruptcy; subsection (1) deals with them.
    WHEN `the rules in bankruptcy relating to contracts of sale` THEN NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this Act affects the enactments relating to bills of sale."
    WHEN `the enactments relating to bills of sale` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of the enactments relating to bills of sale.
    WHEN `some other matter under section 62(3)` THEN NOTHING

-- s 62(4).
-- src:1638 | (4) The provisions of this Act about contracts of sale do not apply to
-- src:1639 | a transaction in the form of a contract of sale which is intended to
-- src:1640 | operate by way of mortgage, pledge, charge, or other security.
@ref s 62(4) (src:1638-1640)
GIVEN `the transaction is in the form of a contract of sale which is intended to operate by way of mortgage, pledge, charge, or other security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 62(4) the provisions of this Act about contracts of sale apply to the transaction` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the transaction is in the form of a contract of sale which is intended to operate by way of mortgage, pledge, charge, or other security`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The provisions of this Act about contracts of sale do not apply to a transaction in the form of a contract of sale which is intended to operate by way of mortgage, pledge, charge, or other security."
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says only that the provisions do not apply to such a transaction.
            NOTHING
